1. docker network create <network name> => to create a network 
2. docker run --network => to attach a container to a network 
3. docker network connect <network> <container> => to connect a container to a network
4. docker inspect <container> => to see details about a container including the networks it's attached to 
5. docker network inspect <network> => to see details about a network 


1. docker compose up -d 
2. docker compose down
https://docs.docker.com/reference/compose-file/


1. dnf install lvm2,  apt install lvm2
2. pvcreate <devname> => to create a physical volume
3. vgcreate <volume group> <pv1> <pv2> etc => to create a volume group 
4. lvcreate -L +size -n <lvname> <vgname>

5. pvs or pvdisaply => to display details about physical volume
6. vgs or vgdisplay => to display details about volume group
7. lvs or lvdisplay => to display details about logical volume

8. vgextend <vgname> <pv> => to add a pv to a volume group
9. lvextend -L +size <vg>/<lv> => to extend a logical volume size
10. resizefs => to resize a file system 
11. lvextend -L +size -r <vg>/<lv> => resize file system while extending the logical volume


